    <item>
      <title>How will a diesel deal with Russia impact the U.S. market?</title>
      <description>The price of diesel hit an all-time high in the U.S. in September. Can President Trump&apos;s deal for Russia to release more diesel onto the market bring the price down?</description>
      <pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:03:37 -0400</pubDate>
      <link>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/nx-s1-6000118/how-will-a-diesel-deal-with-russia-impact-the-u-s-market</link>
      <guid>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/nx-s1-6000118/how-will-a-diesel-deal-with-russia-impact-the-u-s-market</guid>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>The price of diesel hit an all-time high in the U.S. in September. Can President Trump's deal for Russia to release more diesel onto the market bring the price down?</p><img src='https://media.npr.org/include/images/tracking/npr-rss-pixel.png?story=nx-s1-6000118' />]]></content:encoded>
      <dc:creator>Willa Rubin</dc:creator>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>The Trump administration warns Ukraine it could cut off intel, Zelenskyy tells NPR</title>
      <description>Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy sat down for an interview with NPR at a time of renewed tensions with the White House.</description>
      <pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:51:55 -0400</pubDate>
      <link>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/nx-s1-6000051/ukraine-zelenskyy-npr-interview-russia-war</link>
      <guid>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/nx-s1-6000051/ukraine-zelenskyy-npr-interview-russia-war</guid>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<img src='https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5336x4000+330+0/resize/5336x4000!/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fde%2F296b16034475a42491bc86a39366%2Fatc-1340388.jpg' alt='Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy speaks with NPR in Kyiv, Ukraine, on Tuesday.'/><p>Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy sat down for an interview with NPR at a time of renewed tensions with the White House.</p><p>(Image credit: Svet Jacqueline for NPR)</p><img src='https://media.npr.org/include/images/tracking/npr-rss-pixel.png?story=nx-s1-6000051' />]]></content:encoded>
      <dc:creator>Joanna Kakissis</dc:creator>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Government spent millions on Trump ads. And, federal agents raid Ilhan Omar&apos;s home</title>
      <description>The government is using millions of taxpayers&apos; dollars on pro-Trump ads, even after the president said this would not happen. And, federal agents search Rep. Ilhan Omar&apos;s D.C. home.</description>
      <pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 07:08:14 -0400</pubDate>
      <link>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/g-s1-147822/up-first-newsletter-trump-ads-funding-campaign-rallies-ilhan-omar</link>
      <guid>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/g-s1-147822/up-first-newsletter-trump-ads-funding-campaign-rallies-ilhan-omar</guid>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<img src='undefined' alt='President Trump greets supporters during an election rally at the Covelli Centre on Oct. 12, 2026, in Youngstown, Ohio.'/><p>The government is using millions of taxpayers' dollars on pro-Trump ads, even after the president said this would not happen. And, federal agents search Rep. Ilhan Omar's D.C. home.</p><p>(Image credit: Alex Wong)</p><img src='https://media.npr.org/include/images/tracking/npr-rss-pixel.png?story=g-s1-147822' />]]></content:encoded>
      <dc:creator>Brittney Melton</dc:creator>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Pakistan imposes emergency rule in former prime minister&apos;s stronghold</title>
      <description>Pakistan has imposed emergency rule in the province governed by the political party of imprisoned former prime minister Imran Khan.</description>
      <pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 06:51:33 -0400</pubDate>
      <link>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/nx-s1-5998798/pakistan-imposes-emergency-rule-in-former-prime-ministers-stronghold</link>
      <guid>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/nx-s1-5998798/pakistan-imposes-emergency-rule-in-former-prime-ministers-stronghold</guid>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Pakistan has imposed emergency rule in the province governed by the political party of imprisoned former prime minister Imran Khan.</p><img src='https://media.npr.org/include/images/tracking/npr-rss-pixel.png?story=nx-s1-5998798' />]]></content:encoded>
      <dc:creator>Betsy Joles</dc:creator>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Trump&apos;s diesel deal with Putin angers Europe</title>
      <description>President Trump&apos;s diesel deal with Russia sparks European fury, as Ukraine&apos;s President Zelenskyy questions Washington&apos;s motives and allies vow to keep pressure on Moscow.</description>
      <pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 04:44:19 -0400</pubDate>
      <link>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/nx-s1-5998764/trumps-diesel-deal-with-putin-angers-europe</link>
      <guid>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/nx-s1-5998764/trumps-diesel-deal-with-putin-angers-europe</guid>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>President Trump's diesel deal with Russia sparks European fury, as Ukraine's President Zelenskyy questions Washington's motives and allies vow to keep pressure on Moscow.</p><img src='https://media.npr.org/include/images/tracking/npr-rss-pixel.png?story=nx-s1-5998764' />]]></content:encoded>
      <dc:creator>Teri Schultz</dc:creator>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>How NATO plans to combat potential attacks on the alliance from Russia</title>
      <description>NPR&apos;s Steve Inskeep speaks with former U.S. Assistant Secretary for European Affairs Dan Hamilton about NATO&apos;s detailed plans to counter any possible Russian attack on the alliance.</description>
      <pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 04:44:14 -0400</pubDate>
      <link>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/nx-s1-5998721/how-nato-plans-to-combat-potential-attacks-on-the-alliance-from-russia</link>
      <guid>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/nx-s1-5998721/how-nato-plans-to-combat-potential-attacks-on-the-alliance-from-russia</guid>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>NPR's Steve Inskeep speaks with former U.S. Assistant Secretary for European Affairs Dan Hamilton about NATO's detailed plans to counter any possible Russian attack on the alliance.</p><img src='https://media.npr.org/include/images/tracking/npr-rss-pixel.png?story=nx-s1-5998721' />]]></content:encoded>
      <dc:creator>Steve Inskeep</dc:creator>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>DNA and vehicle-tracking help French investigators recover stolen Renoirs</title>
      <description>DNA left on a protective painting cover helped investigators recover two stolen Renoirs and uncover what they suspected were preparations for another art heist, a French prosecutor said Monday.</description>
      <pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 01:42:28 -0400</pubDate>
      <link>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/g-s1-147818/france-stolen-renoirs-recovered</link>
      <guid>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/g-s1-147818/france-stolen-renoirs-recovered</guid>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<img src='https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6192x4128+0+0/resize/6192x4128!/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe7%2Fa7%2F333b7fed483fb4ac1acb61c1ea6a%2Fap26285467970644.jpg' alt='Recovered paintings "Portrait of Madame Colonna Romano", right, and "Young Woman at the Well," stolen from the Renoir Museum in Cagnes-sur-Mer are on display at the Interdisciplinary Centre for the Conservation and Restoration of Heritage in Marseille, France, Monday Oct. 12, 2026.'/><p>DNA left on a protective painting cover helped investigators recover two stolen Renoirs and uncover what they suspected were preparations for another art heist, a French prosecutor said Monday.</p><p>(Image credit: Philippe Magoni)</p><img src='https://media.npr.org/include/images/tracking/npr-rss-pixel.png?story=g-s1-147818' />]]></content:encoded>
      <dc:creator>The Associated Press</dc:creator>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Trump announced a partial Russia-Ukraine ceasefire. Did either country know about it?</title>
      <description>Ukraine&apos;s leader says Russia is continuing to attack Ukraine and is ignoring an &quot;energy ceasefire&quot; declared by President Trump.</description>
      <pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:43:48 -0400</pubDate>
      <link>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/12/nx-s1-5998808/trump-announced-a-partial-russia-ukraine-ceasefire-did-either-country-know-about-it</link>
      <guid>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/12/nx-s1-5998808/trump-announced-a-partial-russia-ukraine-ceasefire-did-either-country-know-about-it</guid>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Ukraine's leader says Russia is continuing to attack Ukraine and is ignoring an "energy ceasefire" declared by President Trump.</p><img src='https://media.npr.org/include/images/tracking/npr-rss-pixel.png?story=nx-s1-5998808' />]]></content:encoded>
      <dc:creator>Charles Maynes</dc:creator>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Many Iranians who go to Turkey to find jobs are exploited</title>
      <description>Desperate Iranians are finding work in Turkey to make ends meet, but many are being exploited and left with  nothing but more debt.</description>
      <pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:37:21 -0400</pubDate>
      <link>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/12/nx-s1-5979836/many-iranians-who-go-to-turkey-to-find-jobs-are-exploited</link>
      <guid>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/12/nx-s1-5979836/many-iranians-who-go-to-turkey-to-find-jobs-are-exploited</guid>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Desperate Iranians are finding work in Turkey to make ends meet, but many are being exploited and left with  nothing but more debt.</p><img src='https://media.npr.org/include/images/tracking/npr-rss-pixel.png?story=nx-s1-5979836' />]]></content:encoded>
      <dc:creator>Hadeel Al-Shalchi</dc:creator>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Both Russia and Ukraine are using AI-powered drones on the battlefield</title>
      <description>A Ukrainian company that got rich making smartphone-controlled cameras to watch pets at home now outfits first-person-view drones with an image recognition system powered by artificial intelligence.</description>
      <pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:42:49 -0400</pubDate>
      <link>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/12/nx-s1-5984940/both-russia-and-ukraine-are-using-ai-powered-drones-on-the-battlefield</link>
      <guid>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/12/nx-s1-5984940/both-russia-and-ukraine-are-using-ai-powered-drones-on-the-battlefield</guid>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>A Ukrainian company that got rich making smartphone-controlled cameras to watch pets at home now outfits first-person-view drones with an image recognition system powered by artificial intelligence.</p><img src='https://media.npr.org/include/images/tracking/npr-rss-pixel.png?story=nx-s1-5984940' />]]></content:encoded>
      <dc:creator>Joanna Kakissis</dc:creator>
    </item>
